# Space Engineers drone printers v{{VERSION}} ({{VARIANT}})

{{INTRO}}

Package contents: {{COUNTS}}. All printers are **dynamic** small-grid ships; **no DLC blocks**.

A printer is a pod (large battery, remote control, Programmable Block running `HiveMotherAI.cs`, gyros, antenna, thrusters in all six
directions) with docking bays on stalks. A bay is a projector `[Bay N]` (the drone blueprint is pre-loaded, Keep Projection on), welders
`[Bay N]` and a merge block `[Bay N]`. The cycle per bay is BUILD (welders on until nothing is left to build), CHARGE (the drone shares
the printer's power and its PB is recompiled), RELEASE (merge blocks off, the printer nudges away, `<Tag>_JOIN` is broadcast) and
COOLDOWN. Printed drones then start working by themselves.

**Timer chain (no script needed):** every bay also has three timers, `Timer Build / Release / Reclamp [Bay N]`. Press `Start` on `Timer Build [Bay N]`
once and the bay loops on timers alone: welders off after the build time, the printer's merge block off (the drone's own LAUNCH block sees it and flies
off), merge block and welders on again after 30 s. Use it when the printer's script is missing or has stopped; while one of a bay's timers counts down
the script leaves the bay alone. The delays are guesses (a timer cannot see when a print is finished): tune `Timer Build`. `Stop` on any timer ends the loop.

**Free lanes:** the drone's path straight ahead (16 cells = 8 m) and its exit lane (9 m) are kept free of welders and scaffold, so a printed drone can take off
nose first. Details: `docs/printer-release.md`.

